        "PsA lacks preceding infectious trigger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "diseaseId": "ankylosing-spondylitis",
      "distinguishingFeatures": [
        "AS has insidious onset without infectious trigger",
        "AS has symmetric sacroiliitis",
        "AS is chronic and progressive from onset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "diseaseId": "ehlers-danlos-hypermobile",
      "distinguishingFeatures": [
        "hEDS has generalized hypermobility without inflammatory arthritis",
        "hEDS has normal inflammatory markers",
        "hEDS is chronic, not post-infectious"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "redFlags": [
    "Purulent joint effusion (exclude septic arthritis)",
    "Acute monoarthritis with crystals on polarized microscopy (gout/pseudogout)",
    "Severe uveitis (urgent ophthalmology referral)",
    "Chronic recurrent course (>6 months) suggesting evolution to chronic SpA",
    "HIV risk factors (reactive arthritis can be severe and treatment-resistant in HIV)"
  ],
